    "1. Phylum Arthropoda (Largest Phylum): Over two-thirds of all named species on earth. Characterized by jointed appendages, a tough chitinous exoskeleton, body division into Head, Thorax, and Abdomen, open circulatory system, and respiratory organs including gills, book gills, book lungs, and tracheal systems. Excretion via Malpighian tubules or Green glands.",
