        "**Phylum Hemichordata Overview:** Formerly considered a subphylum under Chordata, now placed as a separate non-chordate phylum. Consists of a small group of worm-like marine animals with organ-system level of organization, bilateral symmetry, triploblastic, and coelomate body.",
        "**Anatomical Regions & Excretory Organ:** Cylindrical body divided into three distinct anatomical regions: an anterior **Proboscis**, a middle **Collar**, and a long **Trunk**. Respiration occurs through paired **pharyngeal gill slits** (shared feature with chordates). Circulation is open. **Excretion is carried out by a specialized Proboscis Gland**. The collar region contains a hollow outgrowth called **Stomochord** (not a true notochord). Sexes are separate with external fertilization and indirect development via a free-swimming **Tornaria larva**. Examples: *Balanoglossus* and *Saccoglossus*."
